Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","OWASP-A07:2017 - Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)","security"],"precision":"very-high"}},{"id":"javascript.browser.security.open-redirect.js-open-redirect","name":"javascript.browser.security.open-redirect.js-open-redirect","shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: javascript.browser.security.open-redirect.js-open-redirect"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The application accepts potentially user-controlled input `$PROP` which can control the location of the current window context. This can lead two types of vulnerabilities open-redirection and Cross-Site-Scripting (XSS) with JavaScript URIs. It is recommended to validate user-controllable input before allowing it to control the redirection."},"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.browser.security.open-redirect.js-open-redirect","help":{"text":"The application accepts potentially user-controlled input `$PROP` which can control the location of the current window context. This can lead two types of vulnerabilities open-redirection and Cross-Site-Scripting (XSS) with JavaScript URIs. It is recommended to validate user-controllable input before allowing it to control the redirection.\n💎 Enable cross-file analysis and Pro rules for free at sg.run/pro","markdown":"The application accepts potentially user-controlled input `$PROP` which can control the location of the current window context. This can lead two types of vulnerabilities open-redirection and Cross-Site-Scripting (XSS) with JavaScript URIs. It is recommended to validate user-controllable input before allowing it to control the redirection.\n\n#### 💎 Enable cross-file analysis and Pro rules for free at <a href='https://sg.run/pro'>sg.run/pro</a>\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.browser.security.open-redirect.js-open-redirect)\n - [https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/